## Stage 2 — Team Structure

Judges evaluate teams more than ideas. At pre-seed, team quality is the primary signal.

### Ideal Team Composition (2–4 people)
- At least one strong technical founder (can ship fast)
- At least one generalist / product thinker (talks to users, owns narrative)
- No pure project managers — you need executors
- No outsourced development or marketing

### Team Red Flags (any one of these can kill a submission)
- Part-time founders
- Founders not quitting their job for this
- Non-overlapping timezones without strong async discipline
- Majority non-technical team
- Single founder with no explanation (less critical in AI era, but still flagged)
- Unequal equity with no clear rationale
- Team members who cannot speak to the product fluently

### The Relentless Resourcefulness Test
Ask: "If the product broke 2 hours before the demo, what would this team do?"
Winners find a way. Surface this trait explicitly in your submission — in your video, your deck, and your traction story.

