## Stage 6 — Red Flag Audit

Before submitting, run this checklist. A single red flag can end your candidacy.

### Team Audit
- [ ] All founders are full-time on this
- [ ] Technical co-founder can ship independently
- [ ] Everyone can explain the product in simple words
- [ ] Equity split is reasonable and documented
- [ ] Team size is 2–4

### Deck Audit
- [ ] No slide exceeds 20 words
- [ ] No buzzwords present
- [ ] Problem is specific and human
- [ ] Demo link works and loads fast
- [ ] Competition section is honest (you do not win on every dimension)
- [ ] No vanity metrics (social follows, impressions without conversion)

### Idea Audit
- [ ] Blockchain is necessary, not decorative
- [ ] One problem, one solution, one user
- [ ] Market is real and sized honestly

### Story Audit
- [ ] A 12-year-old could understand the pitch
- [ ] A judge on a phone in an Uber could follow it
- [ ] The "why now" is clear
- [ ] The "why us" is clear

---

## Stage 7 — Ecosystem Alignment (Advanced)

Judges are often invested in the Solana ecosystem. Signal awareness.

### Tactics
- If building infra, demo it using a protocol Colosseum has invested in — make the portfolio connection explicit
- If applicable, deploy to Solana Mobile dApp Store (especially if a mobile track sponsor exists)
- Follow judges on X and engage with their content **before** submission deadline — create familiarity
- Ask judges for feedback before the deadline; most will respond and it creates a relationship
- Seek support from Superteam chapters (global, free)
- Build in public: share progress updates, not just the finished product

### Colosseum's Investment Thesis
Read and internalize their blog: https://blog.colosseum.org/
Their thesis is public. Map your project to it explicitly in your submission narrative.

